INSERT INTO `bt_qc_n_c_r_s` VALUES (1,'BT Industrial','Reworked Material',NULL,'- Poor stacking by a BT employee, Forklift driver, during offloading, the driver drove right through the material bag, damaging the bag and quarter of material spill on the floor.','- This was negligence, all forklift drivers have been competently trained, & appointed. \r\n- BT is also performing quarterly task observations.',1,10,'- Waste of company resources (Time & Material)',13,30,'2020-05-13 06:12:41','2020-11-28 14:13:54','2020-04-30','- Perform house keeping, \r\n- Seal the bag','- BT has recalled all forklift drivers to perform a tool box talk, to manly  put emphasis on the issue of awareness during work time, respect of company resources,  good communication skills, truthfulness during investigations, and good stacking and storage, loading and off-loading practices.','NIGHT',1,1,'2020-05-09','- Forklift drivers have been careful during stacking and storage, tool box talks have been of great help.'),(2,'Decon Projetcs','355mm PN12.5',753,'Pipe 1/19 pipes burst during commissioning on site, this was reported to BT industrial on the 15/02/2020,','A sample piece of the pipe that burst was collected by BT Industrial on the 17/02/2019 for investigation, \r\n\r\nThe pipe was measured and the following readings where recorded from the sample piece that was collected,\r\n  \r\nWall thickness readings: (16 points)\r\n\r\nMin: 26.1 mm		Max: 28.71 mm\r\n\r\n1.	24.55 mm	\r\n2.	25.17 mm\r\n3.	25.76 mm\r\n4.	26.68 mm\r\n5.	26.85 mm\r\n6.	26.72 mm\r\n7.	26.4 mm\r\n8.	26.4 mm\r\n9.	26.09 mm\r\n10.	25.4 mm\r\n11.	24.89 mm\r\n12.	25.99 mm\r\n13.	26.68 mm\r\n14.	26.78 mm\r\n15.	26.86 mm\r\n16.	26.7 mm\r\n\r\nTotal average: 26.1195mm (within spec) \r\n\r\n\r\nCause: \r\n\r\nWe suspect 2 ways that which may have caused the failer, \r\n\r\n1.	Material used to manufacture the pipe, (Test were made and the tests results stated below) results: Passed\r\n2.	The failure of a pipe occurs primarily where a pipe bursts as a result of a surge pressure (water hummer), fatigue, or the accumulation of entrapped air, resulting in additional pressures on the pipe wall. \r\n3.	The line did not bleed well through the isolating valves, ensuring air has been removed from the system before closing the bleed valves.\r\n4.	During testing/commissioning, the pressure applied during testing may have been excessive, not applied in accordance to the standards',1,2,'- Waste of material (Raw material, labour force, delivery) costs. (Increase in production costs vs products sold)  \r\n- Downgrading BT\'s brand on customer satisfaction, and quality production.',13,30,'2020-05-13 19:18:04','2020-11-28 14:37:43','2020-02-11','- BT-Industrial communicated with the client regrading the resolution BT Industrial will be taking, \r\n- BT Industrial has therefore replaced the whole order that was manufactured with the batch of material, mainly to maintain the relationship Bt has with the client and as customer satisfaction is our primary role.','','NIGHT',19,2,NULL,''),(3,'PLasti-Tech','355mm PN12.5',789,'- Poor pipe quality, \r\n- No manufacturing markings \r\n- Pipe deformed inside\r\n\r\nQty: x1 off','- Pipe overall quality was caused by the poor water circulation system in the vacuum tank No. 1 on Baila 2 extruder machine, the poor circulation system was caused by water pipes blockage, BT has therefore increased the number of filters its water circulation system to minimize or rather eliminate machine pipe blockages.  \r\n- Manufacturing marking where later found, the marking where laser markings making it difficult to observe from a distance,\r\n\r\nBT Industrial has replaced the poor quality pipe with a more client satisfactory and quality pipe.',1,2,'- Waste of material (Raw material, labour force, delivery) costs. (Increase in production costs)  \r\n- Downgrading BT\'s brand on customer satisfaction, and quality production.\r\n- Scrap rate increase (increasing recycling costs)',13,13,'2020-05-13 20:12:20','2020-08-19 13:47:17','2020-01-25','- BT has replaced the rejected products \r\n- To increase the number of filters\r\n- The pipe that was claimed to have no markings was later found that it does have markings, client didn\'t check initially','- The maintenance team to increase their routine frequency checks on the filtration systems','NIGHT',1,2,NULL,''),(4,'Strata Drilling','HDPE 110mm PN 8 Coils @ 50m long',280,'- x2 coils 110mm PN 8 Coils @ 50m long where found to be 40m long & 44m long.','- Coils where not rolled in accordance with the requirements',1,2,'- Waste of material (Raw material, labour force, delivery) costs. (Increase in production costs vs products sold)  \r\n- Downgrading BT\'s brand on customer satisfaction, and quality production.',13,30,'2020-05-13 20:42:05','2020-11-28 15:30:00','2020-04-25','-An extra 50m long coil has been given to strata drilling to compensate the short lengths','- Ensure the coils rolled are in accordance with the specification. Coils now being weighed to ensure they have correct length.','DAY',2,2,'2020-05-05',''),(6,'Mercury-Inter Trade','HDPE Pipe, 315mm PN10 12m Pipe',1274,'- Pipes where poorly handled by a forklift driver, major scratches where found on the pipe, QC Failed the pipe.','- Negligence during work, loss of focus.',1,7,'Recycling costs increasing.',13,30,'2020-06-09 05:58:06','2020-11-28 17:44:09','2020-05-30','- During the tool box talk, the topic of careful handling during stacking and storage was emphasized. Trained during tool box talks.','- To be alert at all times when driving the forklift.','NIGHT',1,2,'2020-08-18',''),(8,'RamPiping','110mm PN10, 50m coil x1 off, 90mm PN10, 50m coil x1 off, 90mm PN10 6m.',1422,'- 110mm PN10, 50m coil x1 off, kicked on one place.\r\n- 90mm PN10, 50m coil x1 off, - Forklift damage on inside of coil \r\n- 90mm PN10 6m. wall thickness over spec.','- The kinking was the result of poor handling from production to loading are. \r\n- The forklift damage was a result of loading for delivery \r\n- The pipe was not over spec, the client mismatched the ordered pipe vs the requested pipe.',1,10,'- Waste of transport, raw material, (resources) \r\n- Customer dissatisfaction',9,13,'2020-06-23 16:28:24','2020-08-19 13:47:45','2020-06-21','- BT had the products replaced,','- During coil loading the forklift drivers need to inset the pipe sleeves on the forks.','DAY',3,2,NULL,''),(10,'Plasti-Tech - HATCH','HDPE PE 100 PN10 450mm 12m length',1044,'- Object found in the pipe while we facing the pipe. It looks like a grease nipple of some sort.\r\n- As can see our facing tool and blades was damaged. \r\n\r\nPlease have a look at it? As it cause serious QC issues.','- We believe that during the initial cooling stage, the foreign object may have lodged itself into the molten pipe\r\nmaterial before the first phase of cooling was completed. As our screws have sieves to amongst other things protect\r\nthe Screw and Die from damage, such a foreign object could not have entered through the Hopper system.\r\n\r\n- During Quality in-line check, QC final check and client product release, nothing could have been observed as the object was buried within the pipe at that stage.\r\nThis is an extremely rare occurrence and could not have been anticipated. The machine had been running for 5 weeks, which without specific maintenance checks on potentially lose items that may have resulted in this.',0,2,'- Manufacturing costs to increase,',13,13,'2020-07-17 16:26:42','2020-08-19 13:47:53','2020-07-15','- Replacement of the welding dics, Pipe accepted.','-	For all orders running continuously beyond 4 weeks, a short maintenance break will be put in place during production (2 weeks interval) to do minor service & checks on the machine.','DAY',1,2,NULL,'- BT is still awaiting for a quote to replace the welding discs.'),(11,'SABS SANS 4427-2','Product Certification Audit Notification',NULL,'- Lab equipment overdue for calibration','- Lab equipment will be calibrated as notified.',0,5,'- Faults on Lab test results',13,13,'2020-07-29 15:15:42','2020-08-19 13:48:00','2020-07-27','- BT has schedule machine calibration which have expired.','- BT will be automating the inventory list on the ERP system, all machinery that need calibration, an automatic email, one month before expiry will be sent to the HOD to schedule calibration.','Day',NULL,1,NULL,''),(12,'BT-Industrial Group','QC product Handover to Logistics',NULL,'The stock is put into the system by production and there is no handover for dispatch to conform receiving the qtys. This was recorded as non – conformance since dispatch only sees what is in stock when they want to release stock.','- This was noted by BT (Quality & Logistics department) will be developing a system to mitigate the NCR.',1,5,'- Limited product control, potential of products being dispatched without being qualified',13,13,'2020-08-06 10:17:15','2020-08-19 13:48:09','2020-06-30','BT has updated the dispatch process flow and procedure, and included a hold point from QC to Logistics. Only approved products by QC can be released.','Logistics will be requesting product release from QC, QC to approve, then SRN can be printed out.','Day',1,1,'2020-07-06','- The developed system has been working efficiently to date. any deviations or amendment will be recorded.'),(13,'Plasti-tech','HDPE PE 100 PN6 160mm 12m',1546,'- HDPE PE 100 PN6 160mm 12m length has forklift damage,','- The damage was done by a BT forklift driver during loading.',1,10,'- Customer dissatisfaction, leading to a decline in sales.',13,20,'2020-08-06 10:43:07','2020-08-06 14:26:26','2020-08-03','- A replacement pipe was sent to the client','- Forklift forks will be rubberized, to prevent future accidents  \r\n- During tool box talk, the issue of awareness during loading was emphasized to the forklift drivers.','Day',1,2,'2020-08-06','- The client was happy to accept the replacement pipe. \r\n- Ordered has been placed to rabarize the forklift forks'),(14,'Quality Tubes','HDPE PE 100 PN12.5 560mm 12m length',1449,'- Bubbles like form visible on the inside of the pipe when cut.','- This was caused by the material not properly heated in the Hopper mixer, the hopper mixer temperatures where not checked during operations.',1,2,'- Production costs increase\r\n- High scrap rates',13,5,'2020-08-11 12:37:52','2020-08-18 14:30:16','2020-07-22','- Bt has replaced the pipe.','- We have updated our production control measures, on every production document, the hopper mixer temperature will have to be checked by the operator or shift supervisor hourly and record on the production control sheet.','Day',1,2,'2020-08-06','-'),(15,'RENDIfield (PTY) Ltd','HDPE PE 100 PN12.5 160mm 9m length',1674,'-Pipes had deep cuts on them, poor workmanship.','- This was a result of poor handling (forklift)',1,10,'- Scrap percentage increase\r\n- Increase in production costs',13,30,'2020-08-18 08:35:55','2020-11-29 11:35:10','2020-08-09','- Replace the pipes','- Emphasis on product handling during stacking and storage & loading.','Day',2,1,'2020-08-17','-'),(16,'RamPiping Systems (Pty)Ltd','HDPE PE 100 PN10 355mm',1779,'- Pipes were not Laser engraved as per request.','- The laser was giving the operator problems, there was no supervisor so I told him to use ink printer, we couldn’t stop the machine and wait until morning when we could use an alternative printer. I will check the laser and use it in their next orders, we couldn\'t afford to take a chance to let him try and fix because once there is wrong printing we cant delete it, we will have to scrap the pipes\r\n- BT had appointed new operators and had conducted basic training on laser operations.',1,2,'- Customer dissatisfaction',13,5,'2020-08-18 12:10:42','2020-08-18 14:29:57','2020-08-16','- The client has accepted the pipes after explaining the cause of the complain.','- BT will be scheduling a formal laser printer training','Night',28,2,'2020-08-17','-'),(17,'BT-INDUSTRIAL GROUP HDPE','BT-REGRIND (RECYCLING)',NULL,'','',0,5,'',13,NULL,'2020-08-27 11:40:45','2020-08-27 11:40:45','2020-08-25','','','',6840,1,'2020-08-27',''),(18,'Plast-Tech','160mm PN10',1872,'160mm Pn10 pipes marked pn16','Wrong printing since we were running also PN 16 for the same customer.',1,2,'Reallocation of material and funds tied up on the lot before delivery.',13,30,'2020-09-08 11:14:58','2020-11-29 12:17:41','2020-09-04','Pipes were put for the next order PN 16','Attention to detail on job cards  put in place for all operators and supervisors.','DAY',NULL,2,'2020-10-12',''),(19,'Allied  Steelrode','75mm PN10 100mt',2055,'75mm PN10 100mt coils length are under spec instead of 100mt its (90mt - 98mt)','Suspect that the counter encored might be faulty thereby giving false readings',1,2,'Bad reputation which might cause flight of customers',9,9,'2020-10-21 16:27:59','2021-09-09 09:11:44','2020-10-17','we had to buy a wheel counter and calibrate the encoder counter','To use both the encoder and counter wheel as well as validating with weight of each coil to ensure that the length is correct','All',NULL,2,'2020-10-17','we give a customer extra 300mt coils to cover the short length.'),(20,'Allied Steelrode','50mm PN10 100mt',2055,'coils length are under spec instead of 100mt its (90mt - 98mt)','We suspect that the encoder for the counter might be faulty thereby giving wrong reading',1,2,'Bad reputation which might see an exodus of important clients',9,30,'2020-10-21 16:31:17','2020-11-30 09:57:50','2020-10-16','A wheel counter to be purchased and used con-currently with the encoder and validate with length','To frequently calibrate the encoder counter and use the wheel counter as a back up as well weighing each coils to validate the length','All',NULL,2,'2020-10-16','we give the client extra 300mt coils to cover the short fall of all coils'),(21,'mercury','315mm , 450mm and 560mm',3864,'poor handling of the product','when nesting the pipe and offloading them and also reloading the forklift guys had challenges as the pipe were have and when nesting they didn\'t follow the right procedure because they didn\'t lay the ganege on the floor so that they can lay the pipes when nesting them. and some pipes were damaged when offloading,  since they were offloading out side the yard. pipes did fall to the tare road and got scratches as you can see at the beginning of the pipe as the photos shows',1,10,'we can loose customers due to poor workman and BT standard when comes to Quality can drop and the customer will loos faith on use',9,9,'2021-09-08 11:35:02','2022-05-18 07:00:48','2021-09-03','No double when the truck is loaded since we don\'t have a grain. always when nesting we need to lay the pipes on top of the ganage so that the floor doesn\'t scratch the pipe when nesting','we should always follow the loading procedure and communicate with the client if there is double handling that will take place so that they know that some of the pipes will be damaged since we are using forklift','day',63,2,NULL,'BT -Industrial will compensate the pipe meters that are effected accordingly');
